FreeWnn source and patch provenance
===================================

This Debian reintroduction candidate uses the FreeWnn 1.1.1-a023 source
recorded by upstream commit fa30218caa2fe0a90a81b71b85f27814906166f4.
The upstream portability reference is pinned by commit
597e838fc31b3a863a353a823fdd10132681e2e9.

Patch organization
------------------

The active quilt series contains 35 logical patches.  The first 31 patches are
upstream-derived portability changes.  Applying those 31 patches to the a023
base reproduces the pinned upstream reference exactly, apart from generated
configure.  The remaining four patches are Debian-specific supplements:

* 0050 defines MAXPATHLEN on systems that do not provide it;
* 1000 selects Debian filesystem locations;
* 1001 corrects manual-page sections;
* 1002 escapes the atod -s option in roff input.

Historical Debian patches that are empty, obsolete, already included upstream,
or superseded by this logical series are not retained as inactive files.

Generated configure policy
--------------------------

Quilt patches modify configure.in where required and never carry generated
configure.  Debian packaging must regenerate configure with autoreconf.

Task 1 verification
-------------------

The external Task 1 v3.1 verifier checks:

* the exact patch directory and series;
* DEP-3 syntax, exact upstream commit attribution, and rewritten-SHA exclusion;
* the exact 37-commit range from a023 to the pinned upstream tip;
* fuzz-zero application of both the upstream subset and complete series;
* source-tree equality with the pinned upstream tip, excluding generated
  configure;
* patch-header and resulting-source whitespace;
* four separate builds using Debian 13's default gcc with -std=gnu23,
  including full-client and explicit pkg-config terminal-library profiles.

The -std=gnu23 option is a portability-test condition only.  It is not a Debian
package build flag and must not be added to debian/rules or package CI, so the
source package remains backportable to distributions with older compiler
defaults.

Scope
-----

Task 1 only establishes the source patch series.  It does not assert Debian
acceptance, licensing approval, adopter or maintainer commitment, policy
completion, or upload readiness.
